# GitHub → HostGator deploy

**Edit → push to GitHub → live in ~15 seconds.** No manual cPanel uploads.

When the user asks to **push to GitHub**, **deploy**, or **publish**:

1. Commit pending changes if they asked to include them (or changes are part of the task).
2. Push to **`main`** on `origin`: https://github.com/wyatt-winters/BellsPlumbingUtah.git
3. GitHub Actions runs **Deploy to production** (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`):
   - FTPS to `192.254.188.195:21` → `/home1/agentors/public_html/website_302faf96/`
   - Wakes blog bot after upload
4. Confirm deploy started: https://github.com/wyatt-winters/BellsPlumbingUtah/actions

Do **not** run manual FTP unless GitHub Actions is broken.

**Local path:** `/Users/paden/Documents/sites/Bells Plumbing`  
**Live site:** https://bellsplumbingutah.com  
**Secrets (GitHub):** `FTP_USERNAME`, `FTP_PASSWORD`, `BLOG_BOT_KEY`

See `DEPLOY.md` for full pipeline docs.
